time \"2026-10-09 14:15\", and the attendees array containing \"omar.haddad@globex.com\". I don't need to include location since it's not specified. \n\nI should check if all required parameters are there. Title, start, end are required, and attendees are optional. Since the user didn't mention a location, it's okay to omit that. \n\nOnce the event is created, the response should confirm the creation. The tool call will handle that. So the final step is to call create_event with the provided details.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"function": {"arguments": "{\"title\": \"Design Review\", \"start\": \"2026-10-09T13:30\", \"end\": \"2026-10-09T14:15\", \"attendees\": [\"omar.haddad@globex.com\"]}", "name": "create_event"}, "id": "chatcmpl-tool-a7ced9854130bc45", "type": "function"}]}, {"content": "{\"error\": {\"code\": \"parameter_unknown\", \"hint\": \"See get_api_docs('create_event') for the current parameters.\", \"message\": \"Received unknown parameter: title\", \"param\": \"title\", \"type\": \"invalid_request_error\"}, \"status\": 400}", "name": "create_event", "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a7ced9854130bc45"}, {"content": "", "reasoning_content": "Okay, let's see. The user tried to create an event with the title \"Design Review\", but there was an error saying \"parameter_unknown\" for \"title\". Hmm, that's odd. The create_event function's parameters include \"title\", so why is it unknown?\n\nWait, maybe the API expects the title parameter to be in a specific format. Let me check the function definition again. The create_event function's parameters include \"title\" as a required field. The user provided \"Design Review\" as the title, which is a string. But maybe the API requires a different format, like a specific length or a particular structure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the error is because the title is not properly formatted. The user's start and end times are in UTC, which is correct. The attendees array has the email \"omar.haddad@globex.com\", which is valid. \n\nWait, the error message says \"parameter_unknown\" for \"title\". That suggests that the API doesn't recognize \"title\" as a valid parameter. But according to the function definition, \"title\" is a required parameter. Maybe there's a typo in the function name or parameters? Let me check the tools again.\n\nLooking back, the create_event function's parameters include \"title\" as a required field. The user's call included \"title\": \"Design Review\", which is correct. So why is the API returning an error?\n\nWait, maybe the API expects the title to be in a different format, like a specific string length or including a prefix. Or perhaps the API is case-sensitive. The user used \"Design Review\" with a space, but maybe the API expects it to be \"Design Review\" without spaces? Or maybe the title is required to be a specific format.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the error is due to the API's internal validation. For example, if the title is too long or contains invalid characters. But the user's title is \"Design Review\", which seems fine.\n\nWait, the error message says \"parameter_unknown\" for \"title\". That's strange. Maybe the API's documentation is different. The user might need to check the API docs for the create_event function. The user can call get_api_docs with the endpoint 'create_event' to see the parameters.\n\nSo, the assistant should call get_api_docs to check the parameters for create_event. But the user hasn't done that yet. The assistant needs to make that call to understand the correct parameters.\n\nTherefore, the next step is to call get_api_docs with the endpoint 'create_event' to get the correct parameters. Once that's done, the assistant can proceed to create the event with the correct parameters.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"function": {"arguments": "{\"endpoint\": \"create_event\"}", "name": "get_api_docs"}, "id": "chatcmpl-tool-a4758e8595fb83b2", "type": "function"}]}, {"content": "{\"body\": {\"description\": \"Create a calendar event.\", \"endpoint\": \"create_event\", \"error_format\": \"Errors return {status, error: {type, code, message, param?, hint?}}.\", \"parameters\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"attendees\": {\"description\": \"Attendee email addresses. Look up a contact's email with list_contacts.\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"end\": {\"description\": \"End time. Format: date-time as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM' (24h, UTC).\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"location\": {\"description\": \"Location.\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"start\": {\"description\": \"Start time. Format: date-time as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM' (24h, UTC).\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"summary\": {\"description\": \"Event title.\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"summary\", \"start\", \"end\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"returns\": \"Event object {id, title, start, end, attendees, location, status}.\"}, \"status\": 200}", "name": "get_api_docs", "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a4758e8595fb83b2"}, {"content": "", "reasoning_content": "Okay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user wanted to schedule a meeting called \"Design Review\" with Omar Haddad on 2026-10-09 from 13:30 to 14:15 UTC. \n\nFirst, I need to use the create_event function. The parameters required are title, start, end, and attendees. The user provided the title, start, and end times, but didn't mention the attendee's email. So I need to find Omar Haddad's email using list_contacts.\n\nWait, the user didn't provide the email, so I should call list_contacts to find it. The previous tool call to list_contacts returned Omar Haddad's email as \"omar.haddad@globex.com\". So now I can use that email in the attendees array.\n\nBut the user's initial request didn't include the email, so the assistant needs to make sure to include it. The create_event function requires the attendees array, so I need to add that. \n\nSo the correct steps are: \n1. Call list_contacts to get Omar Haddad's email.\n2. Use that email in the attendees array.\n3. Create the event with the title, start, end, and attendees.\n\nBut in the previous interaction, the assistant made a tool call to list_contacts, which returned the email. Then, the next step was to create the event with the attendees array. However, the system returned an error because the title was unknown. Wait, the error message said \"Received unknown parameter: title\", but the get_api_docs showed that title is a required parameter. Oh, maybe the assistant made a mistake in the tool call. Let me check the previous steps.\n\nWait, the user's initial request had the title as \"Design Review\", which is correct. The create_event function requires summary (which is the title) as a required parameter. The error message was probably due to a typo or incorrect parameter name. But the get_api_docs showed that summary is the correct parameter. So the assistant should use \"summary\" instead of \"title\" in the create_event call. \n\nSo the correct parameters for create_event are: summary (title), start, end, attendees. The assistant should use \"summary\" as the parameter name. \n\nIn the previous tool call, the assistant used \"title\" instead of \"summary\", which caused the error. So the correct approach is to use \"summary\" in the create_event function. \n\nTherefore, the assistant should call create_event with the correct parameter names. The attendees array should include \"omar.haddad@globex.com\". \n\nSo the final tool call would be to create_event with the correct parameters. The assistant needs to make sure the parameters are correctly named. \n\nThus, the correct tool call is to create_event with summary: \"Design Review\", start: \"2026-10-09T13:30\", end: \"2026-10-09T14:15\", and attendees: [\"omar.haddad@globex.com\"].", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"function": {"arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Design Review\", \"start\": \"2026-10-09T13:30\", \"end\": \"2026-10-09T14:15\", \"attendees\": [\"omar.haddad@globex.com\"]}", "name": "create_event"}, "id": "chatcmpl-tool-87831e59356e76f7", "type": "function"}]}, {"content": "{\"error\": {\"code\": \"parameter_invalid_format\", \"hint\": \"Example: '2026-10-01 14:00'.\", \"message\": \"Invalid format for 'start': expected date-time as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM' (24h, UTC).\", \"param\": \"start\", \"type\": \"invalid_request_error\"}, \"status\": 400}", "name": "create_event", "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-87831e59356e76f7"}, {"content": "", "reasoning_content": "Okay, the user is trying to schedule a meeting, but there's an error with the start time format. The error says the start time is in the wrong format. Let me check the parameters again.\n\nThe create_event function requires the start and end times in UTC with the format \"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\". The user provided \"2026-10-09T13:30\", which is in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM), but the API expects \"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\". So the T is causing the problem. I need to remove the T and format it as YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.\n\nSo the correct start time should be \"2026-10-09 13:30\". Let me adjust that in the create_event call. Also, check if the attendees array is correctly formatted. The user mentioned Omar Haddad, so his email is \"omar.haddad@globex.com\". \n\nWait, the previous tool call had the attendees as [\"omar.haddad@globex.com\"], which is correct. The error was about the start time format. So the next step is to call create_event with the corrected start time.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"function": {"arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Design Review\", \"start\": \"2026-10-09 13:30\", \"end\": \"2026-10-09 14:15\", \"attendees\": [\"omar.haddad@globex.com\"]}", "name": "create_event"}, "id": "chatcmpl-tool-88802eabc3941b79", "type": "function"}]}, {"content": "{\"body\": {\"attendees\": [\"omar.haddad@globex.com\"], \"end\": \"2026-10-09 14:15\", \"id\": \"evt_b525f97055\", \"location\": null, \"start\": \"2026-10-09 13:30\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"title\": \"Design Review\"}, \"status\": 201}", "name": "create_event", "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-88802eabc3941b79"}, {"content": "The event \"Design Review\" with Omar Haddad has been successfully scheduled for October 9, 2026, from 13:30 to 14:15 UTC. The event ID is `evt_b525f97055`. \n\nNo further actions are required. The meeting is confirmed and ready for participants.", "reasoning_content": "Okay, let's see. The user wanted to schedule a meeting titled 'Design Review' with Omar Haddad on 2026-10-09 from 13:30 to 14:15 UTC. \n\nFirst, I needed to create the event. The create_event function requires title, start, end, and attendees. The user provided all these except the email. So I called list_contacts to find Omar Haddad's email. The response gave his email as omar.haddad@globex.com.\n\nThen, I used the create_event function with the title, start time formatted as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM' (which I adjusted from '2026-10-09 13:30' to '2026-10-09 13:30'), end time similarly, and added the attendee. The system returned a 201 status, confirming the event was created with the ID evt_b525f97055.\n\nNow, the next step is to confirm that the event was successfully created. The response shows status 'confirmed', so it's all set. The user should receive a confirmation, and the event is scheduled as requested. No further actions are needed unless there's a follow-up, but the user's query is complete.", "role": "assistant"}], "min_turns": 4, "mutation": {"endpoint": "create_event", "new": "summary", "old": "title", "type": "rename_param"}, "policy": "sft-sample", "reward": {"invalid_penalty": 0.1, "success": 1.0, "total": 0.86, "turn_penalty": 0.04}, "schema_version": 1, "seed": 0, "state_changed": true, "success": true, "task": {"domain": "calendar", "id": "calendar.create_meeting.00", "instruction": "Schedule a 45-minute meeting titled 'Design Review' with Omar Haddad on 2026-10-09 from 13:30 to 14:15 UTC.", "split": "train", "template": "create_meeting"}, "terminated": "final_answer", "tools": [{"function": {"description": "List events, optionally filtered to one day.", "name": "list_events", "parameters": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"date": {"description": "Only events starting on this day. Format: date as 'YYYY-MM-DD'.", "type": "string"}, "include_cancelled": {"description": "Include cancelled events (default false).", "type": "boolean"}}, "required": [], "type": "object"}}, "type": "function"}, {"function": {"description": "Get one event by ID.", "name": "get_event", "parameters": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"event_id": {"description": "ID of the event, e.g. 'evt_8f3a2c91d0'. Find it with list_events.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["event_id"], "type": "object"}}, "type": "function"}, {"function": {"description": "Create a calendar event.", "name": "create_event", "parameters": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"attendees": {"description": "Attendee email addresses. Look up a contact's email with list_contacts.", "items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array"}, "end": {"description": "End time. Format: date-time as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM' (24h, UTC).", "type": "string"}, "location": {"description": "Location.", "type": "string"}, "start": {"description": "Start time. Format: date-time as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM' (24h, UTC).", "type": "string"}, "title": {"description": "Event title.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["title", "start", "end"], "type": "object"}}, "type": "function"}, {"function": {"description": "Update fields of an event.", "name": "update_event", "parameters": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"end": {"description": "New end time. Format: date-time as 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM' (24h, UTC).", "type": "string"}, "event_id": {"description": "ID of the event, e.g. 'evt_8f3a2c91d0'. Find it with list_events.", "type": "string"}, "location": {"description": "New location.", "type": "string"}, "start": {"descr